[size=5][b]Modern NPC Pathing / NPC Pathing NG[/b][/size]
[size=3]Version [b]2.5.0[/b] · Source: [url=https://github.com/SenjuWoo/Modern-NPC-Pathing]GitHub[/url][/size]

[b]Runtime navmesh failsafe[/b] for humanoid NPCs on Skyrim SE/AE, with [b]optional[/b] SkyParkour vault/climb, EVG Animated Traversal marker routes, and follower parkour replay. Stuck NPCs that are actually trying to walk can step around geometry, handle simple doors, vault or climb when SkyParkour is present, route across EVG markers when EVG is present, and only then use a short validated last-resort teleport.

[size=4][b]What this mod does[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Detects NPCs that are [b]trying to walk[/b] but not moving (idle/sandbox/sit/swim/mount ignored)
[*]Optional [b]SkyParkour[/b] vault/climb for NPCs (needs SkyParkour V3 + its behavior patch)
[*][b]Followers[/b] can replay [i]your[/i] recent SkyParkour moves (teammate flag — NFF / vanilla / similar)
[*][b]EVG Animated Traversal markers[/b] are used as routes (on by default): a stuck NPC parkours along the marker's heading, or hops across to a collision-validated landing
[*][b]Doorway-aware[/b] handling — does not shove NPCs sideways out of chokepoints
[*][b]Last-resort[/b] sidestep teleport only after repeated stuck cycles against static geometry (disableable)
[*][b]MCM[/b] via MCM Helper, or INI without it
[*][b]FOMOD[/b] installer auto-detects SkyParkour and installs a matching INI profile
[/list]

[size=4][b]What this mod does NOT claim[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]EVG Animated Traversal is NOT required[/b]. With it installed, markers work for NPCs as routes since 2.5.0 — never as furniture (the engine rejects NPC furniture entry). Without it, nothing changes. Your player-side EVG use is unaffected.
[*]Not a full AI or pathfinding overhaul
[*]Default max climb is [b]130[/b] units (steps / vaults / low ledges). Raise toward 250 in MCM if you want higher climbs
[*]Indoor parkour is [b]off by default[/b]
[*]SkyParkour climb sounds are 2D. NPCs farther than [b]1600[/b] units will not parkour (MCM: Parkour Max Distance)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[b]Required[/b]
[list]
[*]Skyrim SE (1.5.97) or AE (1.6.x)
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE64[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url]
[/list]

[b]Optional[/b]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/132292]SkyParkour V3[/url] + Nemesis/Pandora (or equivalent) behavior patch — parkour + follower replay
[*]SkyUI + [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/53000]MCM Helper[/url] — in-game settings
[/list]

[b]Not required[/b]
[list]
[*]EVG Animated Traversal
[/list]

[i]NPCPathingNG.esp is ESL-flagged.[/i]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Use a mod manager. Prefer the [b]FOMOD[/b] archive so the installer can pick SkyParkour vs failsafe-only profiles.

[size=4][b]Updating[/b][/size]
Replace the previous version. FormIDs, ESP globals and record layout are unchanged since 2.4.6. A clean save is not required. 2.5.0 only flips the EVG marker-route default from OFF to ON; existing saves keep their saved MCM values.

[b]If you installed yanked 2.4.5:[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Install 2.4.8 or later
[*]Remove leftover [font=Courier New]Data/Scripts/NPNG_MCMBridge.pex[/font] if present
[*]An empty second MCM entry may remain on saves that already loaded 2.4.5 until cleaned or a new game
[/list]

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]MCM: [b]NPC Pathing NG[/b]
[*]INI fallback: [font=Courier New]Data/SKSE/Plugins/NPCPathingNG.ini[/font]
[*]Defaults: followers on, combat NPCs on, indoor parkour off, climb 130, parkour max distance 1600, EVG marker routes on
[/list]

[size=4][b]Changelog (recent)[/b][/size]
[b]2.5.0[/b] — EVG markers as routes (on by default): marker-guided SkyParkour, then a bounds-validated landing hop (ladders/ledges up, drops/rolls down, squeezes/vaults across). The engine-rejected furniture-activation path is removed; marker scanning re-arms on cell change. No save cleaning needed.
[b]2.4.10[/b] — Fixed phantom SkyParkour climb sounds (2D SFX from off-screen / distant NPCs). Parkour now requires the NPC to be within 1600 units of you (MCM: Parkour Max Distance; 0 = unlimited).
[b]2.4.9[/b] — City performance: crowd-jam early-out, EVG cell skip, fruitless-scan latch, cached follower faction.
[b]2.4.8[/b] — First genuine native rebuild since 2.4.4; no more vaults onto barrels/crates; INI/FOMOD preset seeds the MCM.
[b]2.4.6[/b] — Fixed double MCM from 2.4.5.
[b]2.4.5[/b] — [s]Yanked[/s] — do not use.

Full history: [url=https://github.com/SenjuWoo/Modern-NPC-Pathing/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md]CHANGELOG.md[/url]

[size=4][b]Logs / troubleshooting[/b][/size]
[font=Courier New]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE/NPCPathingNG.log[/font]

When reporting issues, include game version, SKSE version, this mod version, whether SkyParkour is installed, and a log excerpt.

